F. Kelly: quadratic approximation vs exact log growth for a binary bet at a fair price
====================================================================================================
   quadratic: G(c f*)/G* = 2c - c^2 -> c=0.5: 0.75, c=1.5: 0.75, c=2: 0
   price 0.50, truth 0.53: full-Kelly growth 1.801 mnats = KL 1.801 mLL; ratios c=0.5: +0.75 c=1.5: +0.75 c=2.0: -0.01 c=2.5: -1.28
   price 0.50, truth 0.60: full-Kelly growth 20.136 mnats = KL 20.136 mLL; ratios c=0.5: +0.75 c=1.5: +0.73 c=2.0: -0.12 c=2.5: -1.69
   price 0.25, truth 0.28: full-Kelly growth 2.340 mnats = KL 2.340 mLL; ratios c=0.5: +0.76 c=1.5: +0.77 c=2.0: +0.08 c=2.5: -1.02
   price 0.20, truth 0.30: full-Kelly growth 28.168 mnats = KL 28.168 mLL; ratios c=0.5: +0.77 c=1.5: +0.80 c=2.0: +0.23 c=2.5: -0.67
   uncertain edge: true/estimated edge ratio k; optimal stake multiplier under quadratic growth = E[k].
   k ~ N(0.7, 0.3^2): best c 0.70; growth at c=1 +0.40 G*, at best +0.49 G*
   k ~ N(0.5, 0.5^2): best c 0.50; growth at c=1 +0.00 G*, at best +0.25 G*
   k ~ N(1.0, 0.5^2): best c 1.00; growth at c=1 +1.00 G*, at best +1.00 G*
   bet selection (optimizer's curse): truth-minus-market a~N(0,A^2), model error ~N(0,Bm^2) in logit;
   A 0.1 B 0.1 (realisation 0.50) |model-market|>0.0: share bet 1.00, true/estimated edge 0.50
   A 0.1 B 0.1 (realisation 0.50) |model-market|>0.1: share bet 0.48, true/estimated edge 0.50
   A 0.1 B 0.1 (realisation 0.50) |model-market|>0.2: share bet 0.16, true/estimated edge 0.50
   A 0.1 B 0.2 (realisation 0.20) |model-market|>0.0: share bet 1.00, true/estimated edge 0.20
   A 0.1 B 0.2 (realisation 0.20) |model-market|>0.1: share bet 0.65, true/estimated edge 0.20
